  "aspGrahaBody": "Graha Drishti is the aspect a planet casts from its position. Every planet fully aspects the 7th house/planet from itself (a direct, face-to-face influence). In addition, Mars aspects the 4th and 8th, Jupiter the 5th and 9th, and Saturn the 3rd and 10th. Rahu and Ketu are usually given the 5th, 7th and 9th. A planet's aspect colours the planet or house it falls on with its own nature.",
  "aspRashiBody": "Rashi Drishti is a sign-to-sign aspect from Jaimini astrology, independent of which planets sit there. Movable signs aspect fixed signs (except the adjacent one), fixed signs aspect movable signs (except the adjacent one), and dual signs aspect the other dual signs. It is used mainly in Jaimini prediction and for judging relationships between houses.",
  "aspDiffBody": "Graha Drishti is cast by a planet and depends on where that planet sits. Rashi Drishti belongs to the sign itself and applies to whatever is placed in it. Graha Drishti is directional (planet A sees planet B), while Rashi Drishti is usually mutual between the signs. When both point to the same target, the influence is especially strong.",
  "aspPredictBody": "An aspect shows where a planet extends its influence beyond its own house. A benefic aspect (Jupiter, Venus, well-placed Moon/Mercury) supports and protects the target; a malefic aspect (Saturn, Mars, Sun, Rahu, Ketu) can pressure, delay or challenge it. Reading which planets aspect a house or planet explains why results appear the way they do.",
